    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4209" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Astyănax</span></b> ,
		actis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀστυάναξ</span> (acc. Gr. Astyanacta, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 2,
		457</span></i>). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Son of Hector and Andromache; at the destruction of
				Troy he was thrown from a tower by Ulysses</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 2,
				457</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13, 415</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A tragic actor in the time of Cicero</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				4, 15, 6</span></i>.</div>
